WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.996 --> 00:00:09.898
"Ha-ha!" At first Scrooge saw only blackness, but then the sound of a man's laughter rang out.

2
00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:14.760
"That laugh sounds familiar," Scrooge thought.

3
00:00:28.484 --> 00:00:32.545
Soon his vision cleared, and he saw that he was in a bright room filled with people.

4
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:37.406
His nephew, Fred, was holding his belly, laughing heartily.

5
00:00:40.187 --> 00:00:43.888
His laughter was contagious, and soon his wife started laughing too.

6
00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:49.910
So did the other people gathered in the room, adults and children alike.

7
00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:58.052
said that Christmas was a humbug and dismissed me," Fred said.

8
00:00:59.084 --> 00:01:00.005
"Can you believe it?"

9
00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:03.407
"That's what I said earlier!"

10
00:01:03.848 --> 00:01:04.888
Scrooge realized.

11
00:01:06.309 --> 00:01:07.810
Was Fred talking about him?

12
00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:14.215
"I can believe he'd say those things," his wife said, her laughter fading.

13
00:01:14.235 --> 00:01:17.517
"That man can't see the good in anything."

14
00:01:20.339 --> 00:01:25.623
Scrooge was startled to hear Fred's wife insult him that way, as she was generally a kind and

15
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:26.484
polite woman.

16
00:01:28.384 --> 00:01:31.547
"He's a comical old fellow, that's the truth," Fred said.

17
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:35.390
"He's not as pleasant or as kind as he could be, that's for sure.

18
00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:38.053
However, I try not to judge others."

19
00:01:40.094 --> 00:01:42.016
His wife's sister rolled her eyes.

20
00:01:42.036 --> 00:01:45.459
"I'll judge Ebenezer Scrooge for you then.

21
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.922
His only good quality is his wealth!"

22
00:01:51.324 --> 00:01:52.165
Fred shrugged.

23
00:01:52.185 --> 00:01:55.188
"My uncle's wealth is of no use to him.

24
00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.381
He doesn't do any good with it.

25
00:01:59.322 --> 00:02:01.383
He doesn't even make himself comfortable with it.

26
00:02:02.404 --> 00:02:07.627
He lives in that small, dreary apartment and hoards his money, which can't possibly make him happy."

27
00:02:07.647 --> 00:02:11.710
"I have no patience with him," his wife said.

28
00:02:12.651 --> 00:02:15.273
Her sister and several others nodded their agreement.

29
00:02:16.854 --> 00:02:17.994
Fred smiled at them.

30
00:02:18.014 --> 00:02:21.997
"I feel sorry for him, which means I can't stay very angry with him.

31
00:02:22.998 --> 00:02:25.279
I mean, who suffers from his bad temper?

32
00:02:25.639 --> 00:02:26.060
He does!

33
00:02:27.532 --> 00:02:32.333
For example, he has decided to dislike us, so he won't come and dine with us, even on

34
00:02:32.373 --> 00:02:35.134
Christmas. What's the consequence?

35
00:02:37.355 --> 00:02:41.116
He misses out on a good dinner and some pleasant moments that he might actually enjoy."

36
00:02:41.136 --> 00:02:49.678
"Your uncle's company might do us harm," a young man called out, which made several other guests laugh

37
00:02:49.718 --> 00:02:57.273
again. "I give my poor old uncle the same invitation every year," Fred said, "whether he likes it

38
00:02:57.313 --> 00:02:57.713
or not.

39
00:02:58.894 --> 00:03:02.117
I certainly don't make his mood any worse by showing up at his office."

40
00:03:03.378 --> 00:03:04.319
His wife nodded.

41
00:03:04.339 --> 00:03:06.000
"That's true.

42
00:03:07.181 --> 00:03:08.803
His mood is always foul!

43
00:03:09.844 --> 00:03:14.488
It's a shame that your kindness, though, doesn't inspire him to help his poor clerk somehow."

44
00:03:16.209 --> 00:03:19.432
"Speaking of Bob Cratchit, I saw him earlier today," Fred said.

45
00:03:19.452 --> 00:03:23.576
"He was carrying that little son of his, the one they call Tiny Tim."

46
00:03:25.612 --> 00:03:28.093
"Oh, that poor boy," a woman said.

47
00:03:28.113 --> 00:03:31.595
"He's been sickly since the day he was born.

48
00:03:32.335 --> 00:03:34.056
But he's such a sweet child!"

49
00:03:34.076 --> 00:03:36.677
"Indeed he is."

50
00:03:37.837 --> 00:03:38.797
Fred shook his head.

51
00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:43.339
"Today Tiny Tim couldn't stop talking about seeing the ice skaters in the park.

52
00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.041
And he told me all about a big turkey in one of the shops."

53
00:03:48.181 --> 00:03:51.643
Fred smiled briefly before his expression went serious again.

54
00:03:51.663 --> 00:03:54.644
"Tiny Tim didn't look well.

55
00:03:55.796 --> 00:03:57.678
I fear the boy doesn't have long to live."

56
00:03:59.999 --> 00:04:04.183
His wife turned to gaze at their own children, who were playing at the other end of the

57
00:04:04.223 --> 00:04:09.087
room. "Oh no," she said softly.

58
00:04:10.568 --> 00:04:13.750
She brushed away a few tears before turning back to the others.

59
00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:18.474
"Fred, we've turned things far too solemn for Christmas.

60
00:04:19.775 --> 00:04:20.836
Let's have some fun."

61
00:04:23.516 --> 00:04:40.129
Scrooge watched as the group played music and sang songs After that, everyone played games, with the children

62
00:04:40.189 --> 00:04:40.710
joining in.

63
00:04:42.471 --> 00:04:46.814
Scrooge had always been impatient with games, which he considered a waste of time.

64
00:04:48.195 --> 00:04:53.944
But tonight he couldn't stop himself from smiling as Fred and his guests enjoyed themselves.

65
00:04:56.106 --> 00:04:58.208
One of the games was called Yes and No.

66
00:04:59.289 --> 00:05:03.593
Fred announced that he was thinking of something, and that the others had to figure out what it

67
00:05:03.653 --> 00:05:09.177
was. However, he could only answer their questions with a simple "yes" or "no."

68
00:05:09.197 --> 00:05:11.820
"Are you thinking of a beast?"

69
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.441
a tall woman called out.

70
00:05:13.461 --> 00:05:16.404
"Yes!" Fred replied.

71
00:05:18.056 --> 00:05:20.077
"Is it something we might serve for dinner?"

72
00:05:20.097 --> 00:05:25.799
"No!" "Is it a savage animal?"

73
00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.281
"Yes!" "Does it grunt?"

74
00:05:32.402 --> 00:05:36.043
"Yes!" "Is it scary?"

75
00:05:36.524 --> 00:05:37.904
a child asked with a shiver.

76
00:05:37.924 --> 00:05:43.046
"Yes!" "I know who it is!"

77
00:05:44.547 --> 00:05:46.848
Fred's sister-in-law clapped her hands and grinned.

78
00:05:47.824 --> 00:05:50.246
"I know exactly the beast you're thinking of, Fred!

79
00:05:51.167 --> 00:05:53.068
It's your uncle Scrooge!"

80
00:05:57.491 --> 00:06:01.854
Everyone at the party, including Fred, burst into loud laughter.

81
00:06:03.275 --> 00:06:04.556
But Scrooge frowned.

82
00:06:05.997 --> 00:06:09.059
Fred's sister-in-law had just called him a scary beast!
